        "statement": "Let $\\mathcal N:\\mathcal L(A)\\to\\mathcal L(B)$ be a finite-dimensional channel, let $d=\\dim A$, and let $\\rho$ be a state on $A$. Fix a finite Stinespring dilation of $\\mathcal N$ and its complementary channel. For each integer $n\\ge1$ there is an exact decomposition $\\rho^{\\otimes n}=\\sum_t p_t\\tau_t$ into mutually orthogonal flat spectral-type states, with at most $(n+1)^d$ positive-weight types and $H(T):=-\\sum_{t:p_t>0}p_t\\ln p_t\\le d\\ln(n+1)$. For the fixed complement and its tensor powers, $$\\sum_t p_t I_c(\\tau_t,\\mathcal N^{\\otimes n})\\ge nI_c(\\rho,\\mathcal N)-H(T),$$ $$\\sum_t p_t[S(\\tau_t)+I_c(\\tau_t,\\mathcal N^{\\otimes n})]\\ge n[S(\\rho)+I_c(\\rho,\\mathcal N)]-2H(T).$$ Thus in each inequality some flat type state attains at least the displayed lower bound.",
